content.text:
You’re right: `twyne.love` should be fixed at the frontend/site layer. Convex is only relevant if we want the sitemap to automatically enumerate Convex-backed published articles.

So I’ll scope the fix to:

- direct `/robots.txt` and `/sitemap.xml` frontend responses;
- correct canonical URLs and trailing-slash behavior;
- the existing frontend pages listed in the sitemap;
- no new Convex query or backend changes.

That will improve indexing for the actual static frontend pages. Dynamic writer/article pages would need a separate URL source later if you want them included automatically.

